WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.647
Step five applies against the
fake, with the same run I D,

2
00:00:03.647 --> 00:00:07.563
so it sends exactly the nineteen
requests the dry run wrote.

3
00:00:07.563 --> 00:00:11.001
It prints the same read,
plan and findings, then:

4
00:00:11.001 --> 00:00:15.887
nineteen requests sent, and after
a fresh read, zero left to change.

5
00:00:15.887 --> 00:00:18.400
Step six shows the code refusing.

6
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:22.512
Build a client for the read task, and
try to write a policy update with it.

7
00:00:22.512 --> 00:00:25.847
It throws: that call isn't
declared for the read task;

8
00:00:25.847 --> 00:00:28.150
add it to the call list with its role.

9
00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:29.838
A read client can't write.

10
00:00:29.838 --> 00:00:32.875
Then ask the code to treat
a web app as a scope.

11
00:00:32.875 --> 00:00:38.338
It refuses: a scope must be a management
group, a subscription or a resource group.

12
00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:41.770
Step seven runs the tests,
three hundred thirty pass,

13
00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:43.990
and you delete the output folder.
